---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="Marc-Olivier Arsenault, technical data leader and author of Coffee and Data.">
  <div class="narrow">
    <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The person behind the notebook</p><h1>Hi, I’m Marc-Olivier.</h1></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="about-intro">I’m a technical data leader.</p>
      <p>Coffee and Data is where I share what I learn about data, engineering, and the people doing the work.</p>
      <p>My background spans data science and data engineering. I care about building useful data assets, helping teams do better work, and solving real problems.</p>
      <p>At the end of the day, what we build is about people. Technology is how we get there.</p>
      <p>You can find my projects on <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a> or connect with me on <a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
      <h2>A note on the quiet years</h2>
      <p>You might notice some quiet years in the archive. It’s not that I ran out of things to say. Work keeps me busy, and so do my kids. I coach their teams, so a lot of my evenings and weekends go to practices and games, not to a keyboard. I write when I have something worth sharing and the time to do it properly, not on a schedule.</p>
      <p>So posts come in waves. If you’d rather not keep checking back, <a href="/subscribe/">subscribe</a> and I’ll let you know when a new one is out.</p>
      <h2>Other notebooks to explore</h2>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thelonenutblog.wordpress.com/">The Lone Nut</a> — a former colleague’s technology blog.</li><li><a href="https://ianwhitestone.work/">Ian Whitestone</a> — writing about data and engineering.</li></ul>
      <h2>A small disclaimer</h2>
      <p>The views on this site are my own and don’t necessarily represent my employer’s positions, strategies, or opinions.</p>
    </div>
    <Newsletter compact id="about-newsletter" />
  </div>
</Base>
